{"authored" [{"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/b771ac7e3d7e724b1eae9ebfc592d36a903a1fc46cc2aac5a55ea9517dc2ce12.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2,3}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x-(-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)(x-3\\text{i})(x+3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}-x(-3\\text{i})-x(3\\text{i})+(3\\text{i})(-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-4)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+9x-4{x}^{2}-36 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cf3a80d009bfbef82c6233d04ec4a7eaf0c49ef6660872e952b071df85ae8053" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-12"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-18"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+16"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x-14"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-17407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+9x-36"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/state.json" "file_sha256" "88ec45055cae15204f9378be68eec604973163650de5acea6129c413881b5bf8" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-8799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-8799.json" "file_sha256" "70b15881bf1aa998c0bac3a555d682ce9717d820d670dd3035bc8d3bbf398a9d" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-8799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-8799.json" "file_sha256" "70b15881bf1aa998c0bac3a555d682ce9717d820d670dd3035bc8d3bbf398a9d" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-5792.json" "file_sha256" "5caa8000ca20e69592f4ec682ca70cc0161c31eb71645f942c86601ea43c591c" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/example-5792.json" "file_sha256" "5caa8000ca20e69592f4ec682ca70cc0161c31eb71645f942c86601ea43c591c" "basis" 831 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,{x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}$x\\,-$\n{{field-4}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c85a19be08a8c2307b20f82feb4e06633d02690ca32e6ed9deb7d6757772ebb" "basis" 886 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-4,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =2(x-(-4))(x-(-4))(x-1) \\\\  & =2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+4)(x+4)(x-1) & =2({x}^{2}+8x+16)(x-1) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+8{x}^{2}-8x+16x-16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+8x-16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{3}+14{x}^{2}+16x-32.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/state.json" "file_sha256" "8c85a19be08a8c2307b20f82feb4e06633d02690ca32e6ed9deb7d6757772ebb" "basis" 886 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "84105d3e3c2789c6fb700d3bfd509a862a2e8fa15a9f73cee39754341118d6c3" "basis" 886 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981281/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981