6" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-316621" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-2(x-(-5))(x-0)(x-1) \\\\  & =-2x(x+5)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x(x+5)(x-1) & =-2x({x}^{2}+4x-5) \\\\  & =-2({x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8787dd3d1106e68f1f6f500c294c5c0c69becc787a3f56eadd807b5847520df4"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+10x"] ["math" "-2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x"] ["math" "-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+5x"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-10x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104469" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+10x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{1}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =1(x-(-1))(x-4)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+1)(x-4)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-4)(x-5) & =({x}^{2}-3x-4)(x-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2}+15x-4x+20 \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8787dd3d1106e68f1f6f500c294c5c0c69becc787a3f56eadd807b5847520df4"} {"question" "q-107681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+8x+9"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+11x+10"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+5x+10"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+x+20"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+11x+20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{2}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $-1.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,$ ${x}_{1}=-4,$ and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =-1(x-(-5))(x-(-4))(x-(-3)) \\\\  & =-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+5)(x+4)(x+3) & =-({x}^{2}+9x+20)(x+3) \\\\  & =-({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+9{x}^{2}+27x+20x+60) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8787dd3d1106e68f1f6f500c294c5c0c69becc787a3f56eadd807b5847520df4"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}-38x-30"] ["math" "-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-19x+30"] ["math" "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+19x+60"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+47x+60"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-104467" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-47x-60"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/a926400e24bc00ca9027d44461e800fa22015ff8289f05fba3a8b51f8b72cce5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=0$ and ${x}_{2,3}=2\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=4.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =4(x-0)(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4x(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(x-(2+2\\text{i}))(x-(2-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-x(2-2\\text{i})-x(2+2\\text{i})+(2+2\\text{i})(2-2\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4x+8) & = \\\\ 4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8787dd3d1106e68f1f6f500c294c5c0c69becc787a3f56eadd807b5847520df4"} {"question" "q-107670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+8x"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+10x"] ["math" "4{x}^{3}-8{x}^{2}+16x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}+32x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5