 =2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-3)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 2(x-3)({x}^{2}-(5\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 2(x-3)({x}^{2}+25) & = \\\\ 2({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+25x-75) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8787dd3d1106e68f1f6f500c294c5c0c69becc787a3f56eadd807b5847520df4"} {"question" "q-107669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+50x+10"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+20x-15"] ["math" "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150"] ["math" "{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+50x+150"] ["math" "{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+25x-75"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "q-107669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+50x-150"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/state.json" "file_sha256" "b97218003d5040869cefa9df1b40539500482f73743419ed51cf01f56c45cb9e"} {"question" "e-8799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The cubic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=x_2=2,x_3=1,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/example-8799.json" "file_sha256" "70b15881bf1aa998c0bac3a555d682ce9717d820d670dd3035bc8d3bbf398a9d"} {"question" "e-8799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_3=1},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-2)(x-1) & =3({x}^{2}-4x+4)(x-1) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}+4x+4x-4) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+8x-4) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^3 -15x^2+24x-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/example-8799.json" "file_sha256" "70b15881bf1aa998c0bac3a555d682ce9717d820d670dd3035bc8d3bbf398a9d"} {"question" "e-5792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/example-5792.json" "file_sha256" "7543c5670c2a4f359872a167917419228aa6d5ad17148488a59c30c1b6682b58"} {"question" "e-5792" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039932/example-5792.json" "file_sha256" "7543c5670c2a4f359872a167917419228aa6d5ad17148488a59c30c1b6682b58"}] "usage" {"e-5792" [] "q-316621" [] "q-104469" [] "e-8799" [] "q-17407" []} "basis" 1395 "retractions" [[17592186278535 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/b771ac7e3d7e724b1eae9ebfc592d36a903a1fc46cc2aac5a55ea9517dc2ce12.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a cubic polynomial $f(x).$\nFind $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$"] [17592186087511 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978465/assets/1c498dcdef2a71cc27117c2c0a43dd54074128ec3e5693e13a12d18b660d1cf4.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $1.$"]] "immutable_answer